[Event "Catalan: Open (4...dxc4)"]

{The Catalan combines the Queen's Gambit with a g2 fianchetto. The bishop on g2 rakes the long diagonal toward b7 and a8, so even a pawn down White often has lasting pressure.}
1. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... Nf6 {Flexible. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
2. c4 {Grabs space. The pawn on c4 controls d5.}
2... e6 {Prepares ...d5 or ...Bb4. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
3. g3 {[%csl Gg2] The Catalan: the bishop will go to g2.}
3... d5 {Classical centre. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls e4.}
4. Bg2 {[%cal Gg2b7] The Catalan bishop aims at the queenside.}
4... dxc4 {The Open Catalan: Black grabs c4.}
5. Nf3 {Develops and covers e5. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
5... Be7 {Solid development.}
 (5... a6 {Tries to hold c4 with ...b5.}
6. O-O {Castles; no hurry to regain the pawn. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... b5 {Holds the pawn.}
7. Ne5 {[%cal Ge5a8] Opens the g2-bishop on the a8 rook. The knight on e5 eyes the pawn on f7 and the pawn on c4.}
7... Nd5 {Blocks the diagonal.}
)
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7. Qc2 {[%cal Gc2c4] Regains the pawn. The queen on c2 eyes the pawn on h7 and the pawn on c4 and controls e4.}
7... a6 {Prepares ...b5.}
8. Qxc4 {Regains the pawn. The queen on c4 eyes the pawn on c7 and the pawn on a6 and controls d5.}
8... b5 {Gains time on the queen. The pawn on b5 eyes the queen on c4.}
9. Qc2 {Retreats, still eyeing c6 and h7. The queen on c2 eyes the pawn on c7 and the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
9... Bb7 {Fights the g2-bishop. The bishop on b7 eyes the knight on f3 and controls d5 and e4.}
10. Bd2 {Prepares Ba5 or Rc1, targeting c7.} *

[Event "Catalan: Closed & 4...Bb4+"]

{Black can keep the centre closed with ...Be7 and ...c6, or give a check on b4 first.}
1. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
1... Nf6 {Flexible. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
2. c4 {Space. The pawn on c4 controls d5.}
2... e6 {Solid. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
3. g3 {Catalan.}
3... d5 {Centre. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls e4.}
4. Bg2 {The long diagonal. The bishop on g2 eyes the pawn on d5 and controls e4.}
4... Be7 {The Closed Catalan.}
 (4... Bb4+ {Gets the bishop out with check. It is check, so the reply is forced.}
5. Bd2 {Blocks and offers a trade. The bishop on d2 eyes the bishop on b4.}
5... Be7 {Retreats; the d2-bishop is a bit passive.}
6. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
6... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... c6 {Solid.}
8. Qc2 {Flexible queen. The queen on c2 eyes the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
)
5. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
5... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... c6 {Supports d5.}
7. Qc2 {Supports e4. The queen on c2 eyes the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
7... Nbd7 {Prepares ...b6 or ...b5. The knight on d7 controls e5.}
 (7... b6 {Straight to the b7 fianchetto.}
8. Bf4 {[%cal Gf4b8] Develops actively, eyeing b8 and the c7 square.}
)
8. Nbd2 {[%csl Ge4] Prepares e4. The knight on d2 controls e4.}
8... b6 {The bishop goes to b7.}
9. e4 {[%cal Ge4d5] The central break. The pawn on e4 eyes the pawn on d5.} *
